  "interpretation": [
    "Weather improves rolling monthly holdout RMSE in 5 of 7 LightGBM folds and 6 of 7 XGBoost folds.",
    "November 2024 is a shared failure month; LightGBM also slightly loses in October 2024.",
    "Pooled out-of-sample RMSE is substantially lower with weather for both model families.",
    "On the Jan-Mar XGBoost feature-group ablation, temperature features alone outperform calendar-only by 48.1% RMSE.",
    "Removing temperature eliminates the weather gain in that holdout, while all-weather improves RMSE by 35.5%.",
    "The one-year result supports a robust retrospective weather-demand association, not causal inference or multi-year forecasting generalization."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "All rolling folds come from one financial year.",
    "Same-day realized ERA5 reanalysis means retrospective prediction, not day-ahead forecasting.",
    "Five representative ERA5 points are equally weighted rather than load weighted.",
    "The feature-group ablation uses XGBoost only.",
    "The feature-group ablation uses 10 Optuna trials per variant and should not be read as a definitive ranking of all possible model configurations.",
    "Holiday and event indicators are absent."
  ]
}
